Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 681acde5f1e30cfdc1a8e21d91a9e6c74f0775cc)

[livepaper: only the GLPlayer half: next-v2 has no WaylandOutputViewport (its frontend, not built for the core, has its own Wayland output); the core's mpv player renders without waiting for the frame target time]

Origin: upstream-PR
Upstream-PR: https://github.com/Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine/pull/677
Adapted-by: livepaper
Why: a host-paced render loop must never sleep inside mpv_render_context_render (video wallpapers / video textures in the core)
Status: upstream: merged on Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine main 2026-10-28, not (yet) on next-v2
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
index a59b63e..ec2ed48 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
@@ -170,9 +170,15 @@ void GLPlayer::render () const {
 
     // no need to flip as it'll be handled by the wallpaper rendering code
     int flip_y = 0;
+    // The host loop is paced by the compositor's frame callbacks (vsync). Do not
+    // let libmpv block until the frame's target time: with several outputs each
+    // owning a player on one thread, that serialises every screen onto the
+    // video's frame grid and judders 24fps content on 60Hz outputs.
+    int block_for_target_time = 0;
 
     mpv_render_param params[] = { { MPV_RENDER_PARAM_OPENGL_FBO, &fbo },
 				  { MPV_RENDER_PARAM_FLIP_Y, &flip_y },
+				  { MPV_RENDER_PARAM_BLOCK_FOR_TARGET_TIME, &block_for_target_time },
 				  { MPV_RENDER_PARAM_INVALID, nullptr } };
 
     mpv_render_context_render (this->m_renderContext, params);
